    "rationale": "Per-round updates show exactly zero update norm in rounds 11, 15 and 17, which is what uploading the global model back without training looks like. GU's other rounds are small-norm updates, consistent with a small site (n_train 708). The exact zeros are the main evidence. The cosine and norm anomalies are noisy because the client is small. Local performance is normal, and the drift and feature flags for GU are weak, so I do not attribute them to a separate fault.",
