  "summary": "Screened all 52 clients on updates, local performance, drift, feature tails, and subgroup outcomes (Sex, AgeGroup, Income), then used the remaining budget to check GU and PR per round. Three clients (GA, IA, WI) show clear sign-flipped, heavily scaled updates in every round (mean cosine about -0.96 to -0.98, norm ratios 10 to 14x) with normal local performance. This is reported as poisoning from round 1. GU shows exact zero-norm updates in rounds 11, 15 and 17, consistent with free-riding; I report it with moderate confidence (0.6) from onset round 11. Other leads did not reach the evidence bar and are not reported: DC (mean_cos z -5.1, BMI outlier with z_noise 4.4), PR (mean_cos z -5.4, normal per-round norms, CITL 0.077 close to the pooled 0.063), NV and OH (subgroup outliers with z_noise below 4), and the drift onsets flagged for small clients (AL, IL, NV, PR, VI), which show no consistent drift. The budget is fully spent (0 remaining)."
